  "format": "ai-tools",
  "script": "Stop asking ChatGPT for a viral script. You get slop, and half of Gen Z say they've unfollowed someone over it.\n\nFive prompts that do work, and every one starts with something only you have. Even OpenAI's own prompts leave a gap that says paste details.\n\nFirst, make a Project, drop in your three best scripts, and tell it to write like those. Free accounts get Projects too.\n\nThen ask what your audience wants to know about your topic, and name them.\n\nPaste your transcript and ask for five hooks, each in a different tone.\n\nAsk for a thirty-second script with narration left and visuals right, so you get a shot list.\n\nTo repurpose, paste a long video's transcript, not the link, and ask for three moments that stand alone as clips.\n\nLeave your material out and you're back to slop. YouTube won't pay for mass-produced AI videos without your own insight.\n\nSave it for the next time you open ChatGPT.",
